  "reply_construction_scope": [
    "Logical replies are freshly constructed codec inputs, not daemon-produced replies or proof of server execution, comparison truth, attr lookup, storage filtering, persistence, limits or permissions.",
    "GET reply value_len=4 and raw outdata are explicitly supplied through public claim_ops, following the audited GET handler shape; native merge_osd_op_vector_out_data independently derives payload_len=4.",
    "GETXATTRS outdata is produced by native ceph::encode on std::map<string,bufferlist,less<>> containing raw name _raw/ff and empty; it is not a Python/Go map encoding.",
    "Native constructor request ops and explicit outdata/results are supplied with public claim_ops. Encoder creates empty-front/data MOSDOpReply payloads; separately decoded objects are never encoded or re-exported.",
    "The mixed GET/GETALL/CMP reply uses aggregate=0 and per-op results 0,0,+1; CMP false is constructed aggregate/per-op -ECANCELED(-125). These raw signed codec cases do not execute a comparison helper.",
    "SET refusal is constructed aggregate/per-op -EFBIG(-27), the audited value-limit handler code. RM refusal is constructed aggregate/per-op -ENOENT(-2), the audited missing-object handler code. No native limit/missing-object invocation is claimed here.",
    "Read-only mixed success uses native ACK completion, with no ONDISK durability claim. Negative SET/RM replies request no completion acknowledgment. Existing live OSD/native state evidence remains separate."
  ],
  "native_decoder_scope": "Separate new MOSDOp/MOSDOpReply objects receive only bytes directly generated by the fresh native encoder; native decode_payload verifies every packed union and request indata/reply outdata and result against encoded native ops. Those decoded objects are never reused as encoder inputs.",
